<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neumarkt in der Oberpfalz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neumarkt in der Oberpfalz is a town in the Upper Palatinate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>. In the 15th century it was the residence of Palatine princes, first of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> John and then, from 1448, of the Palatinate-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosbach">Mosbach</a> line. It later became part of the Electoral Palatinate and in 1628 of Bavaria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neumarkt-in-der-oberpfalz.jpg" alt="Neumarkt in der Oberpfalz" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: pegasus2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neumarkt_Oberpfalz_11052008.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
